    <string name="onboarding_welcome_title">Turn your day into a game</string>
    <string name="onboarding_welcome_text">Finish your habits, dailies and to-dos to earn XP and gold. Miss a daily and you lose some health. Everything stays on your phone: no account, no internet.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_language">Language</string>
    <string name="onboarding_how_title">How it works</string>
    <string name="onboarding_how_habits">Tap + for something good and − for something you want to cut down. As often as you like.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_how_dailies">Repeat on days you choose. Do them to keep your streak, which boosts your XP.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_how_todos">One-off tasks with an optional due date and checklist.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_how_rewards">Spend your gold on treats you define yourself.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_how_warning">If your health reaches zero you lose a level and half your gold, so pause the game for holidays or illness in Settings.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_features_title">Choose your game</string>
    <string name="onboarding_features_intro">These are extras. Leave them on for the full game, or turn off what you do not want. You can change any of them later in Settings.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_feature_quests">Boss quests</string>
    <string name="onboarding_feature_quests_text">Finished tasks hurt a boss, which escapes if you run out of days. Losing one costs you nothing.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_feature_classes">Classes and skills</string>
    <string name="onboarding_feature_classes_text">From level 10, pick a class, spend stat points and cast skills with mana.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_feature_gear">Gear bonuses</string>
    <string name="onboarding_feature_gear_text">Gear from the shop gives small bonuses. Off, it is only for show.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_setup_title">Start with a few tasks</string>
    <string name="onboarding_setup_hint">Untick anything you do not want. You can change all of it later.</string>
